{"duration_api_ms":160601,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d01c6516-f0a0-431f-b183-6d74fbdc675b","total_cost_usd":0.10019699999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9246,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16339,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14166},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9246,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":16339,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9246},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":16339,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9246,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.10019699999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":14166,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"merged_document\": \"# Nimbrel Probe stream name with unsupported symbols\\n\\nAuthor: Rune Delacroix\\nUpdated: 2026-01-29\\n\\n### Topic\\n\\nStream name is a mandatory field for every Nimbrel Probe agent and separates one instrumented process from the next. The stream name cannot contain arbitrary symbols; only letters, digits, spaces and hyphens are accepted. Stream names are validated against the pattern ^[A-Za-z0-9 -]+$ before the agent registers, and if symbols fall outside this set, the agent refuses to start. Examples of refused characters include dots, so `checkout.web` would not be accepted. Documentation on stream name configuration is available for [Java](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/java/current/config-core.html#config-stream-name) and [browser](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/browser/current/configuration.html#stream-name) agents. Some customers need their stream names left unchanged because those strings are product names used throughout their organization and their reporting depends on them.\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\nAll Nimbrel Probe agents\\n\\n### Instructions/Answer\\n\\nThere is no fix at present for this validation restriction. As a workaround:\\n\\n1) Rename the stream to drop the unsupported symbols so the Nimbrel Probe agent will register\\n2) Carry the original name along as a global tag, so each trace keeps a link between the real name and the renamed one, as described in the [configuration documentation](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/nodejs/current/configuration.html#global-tags).\\n\\n{internal-notes}\\nhttps://tickets.nimbrel.example/700Bb00000QrmTD\\nhttps://tickets.nimbrel.example/700Bb00000LnqWs\\n{/internal-notes}\",\n  \"decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"slot\": \"title\",\n      \"candidates\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Nimbrel Probe stream name with unsupported symbols\",\n          \"document\": \"source_a.md\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Nimbrel Probe - dot in stream name is refused\",\n          \"document\": \"source_b.md\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"chosen\": \"Nimbrel Probe stream name with unsupported symbols\",\n      \"reason\": \"Base document title is more general and appropriate\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dispositions\": [\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Stream name is a mandatory field for every Nimbrel Probe agent and separates one instrumented process from the next.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Fixed typo, combined with b5 about process separation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Documentation on stream name configuration is available for [Java](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/java/current/config-core.html#config-stream-name) and [browser](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/browser/current/configuration.html#stream-name) agents.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Combined with b6 to list both agent-specific documentation links\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a6\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Stream names are validated against the pattern ^[A-Za-z0-9 -]+$ before the agent registers, and if symbols fall outside this set, the agent refuses to start.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Code block content converted to prose in topic explanation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Some customers need their stream names left unchanged because those strings are product names used throughout their organization and their reporting depends on them.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Completed incomplete sentence to clarify customer requirement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a11\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"There is no fix at present for this validation restriction. As a workaround:\",\n      \"reason\": \"Phrase incorporated into combined issue and solution introduction\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a13\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Carry the original name along as a global tag, so each trace keeps a link between the real name and the renamed one, as described in the [configuration documentation](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/nodejs/current/configuration.html#global-tags).\",\n      \"reason\": \"Fixed typo orignal→original, reformatted link, improved phrasing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"a14\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"{internal-notes}\\nhttps://tickets.nimbrel.example/700Bb00000QrmTD\\nhttps://tickets.nimbrel.example/700Bb00000LnqWs\\n{/internal-notes}\",\n      \"reason\": \"Merged internal note references from both documents\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b1\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Nimbrel Probe stream name with unsupported symbols\",\n      \"reason\": \"Base title provides more general framing of the issue\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b2\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Author: Rune Delacroix\\nUpdated: 2026-01-29\",\n      \"reason\": \"Base document metadata used for consistency\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b3\",\n      \"disposition\": \"dropped\",\n      \"replacement\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"Section header reorganized; content merged into Topic\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b4\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Examples of refused characters include dots, so `checkout.web` would not be accepted.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specific example integrated into validation explanation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b5\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Stream name is a mandatory field for every Nimbrel Probe agent and separates one instrumented process from the next.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Process separation fact combined with a4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b6\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Documentation on stream name configuration is available for [Java](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/java/current/config-core.html#config-stream-name) and [browser](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/browser/current/configuration.html#stream-name) agents.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Combined with a5 linking both agent type documentation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b7\",\n      \"disposition\": \"dropped\",\n      \"replacement\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"Section header removed; content integrated into Instructions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b8\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reworded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"There is no fix at present for this validation restriction.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Statement expressed as part of workaround section\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b9\",\n      \"disposition\": \"dropped\",\n      \"replacement\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"Section header removed; content merged into Instructions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b10\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"1) Rename the stream to drop the unsupported symbols so the Nimbrel Probe agent will register\\n2) Carry the original name along as a global tag, so each trace keeps a link between the real name and the renamed one, as described in the [configuration documentation](https://docs.nimbrel.example/probe/agent/nodejs/current/configuration.html#global-tags).\",\n      \"reason\": \"Base document provides more complete workaround solution\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b11\",\n      \"disposition\": \"dropped\",\n      \"replacement\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"Section header removed; content merged into Instructions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b12\",\n      \"disposition\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"replacement\": \"\",\n      \"reason\": \"Exact duplicate of b10\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b13\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"{internal-notes}\\nhttps://tickets.nimbrel.example/700Bb00000QrmTD\\nhttps://tickets.nimbrel.example/700Bb00000LnqWs\\n{/internal-notes}\",\n      \"reason\": \"Merged internal note references from both documents\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\"\n}\n```","ttft_ms":145287,"type":